{"@context":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/","id":"P-eee_1045467100313_135436_1","$schema":"https://specif.de/v1.2/schema#","title":[{"text":"CASCaRA Metamodel and Semantic Infrastructure"}],"description":[{"text":"A set of SpecIF Classes derived from a SpecIF Ontology for the domains SpecIF:DomainBase, SpecIF:DomainSystemsEngineering, SpecIF:DomainSystemModelIntegration.","format":"plain","language":"en"}],"generator":"SpecIF Model-Integrator and Editor","generatorVersion":"1.2.a.38","createdAt":"2026-02-24T14:49:03.151Z","rights":{"title":"Creative Commons 4.0 CC BY-SA","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"},"dataTypes":[{"id":"DT-ShortString","changedAt":"2023-05-22T22:51:56.698Z","title":"String <=256","description":[{"text":"Text string with maximum length 256"}],"revision":"1.1","type":"xs:string","maxLength":256},{"id":"DT-Text","changedAt":"2023-05-22T22:54:51.783Z","title":"Plain or formatted Text","description":[{"text":"Text string"}],"revision":"1.1","type":"xs:string"},{"id":"DT-String-LE32","changedAt":"2025-03-06T15:04:02.280Z","title":"String <=32","description":[{"text":"Text string with maximum length 32"}],"revision":"1.1","type":"xs:string","maxLength":32},{"id":"DT-Boolean","changedAt":"2024-07-09T12:03:24.570Z","title":"Boolean Value","description":[{"text":"A Boolean value."}],"revision":"1.2","type":"xs:boolean"}],"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Name","changedAt":"2023-05-22T22:51:56.698Z","title":"dcterms:title","description":[{"text":"<p>A name given to the resource. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title\">DCMI</a></i>)</small></p><p>Title (reference: Dublin Core) of the resource represented as rich text in XHTML content. SHOULD include only content that is valid inside an XHTML 'span' element. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://open-services.net/\">OSLC</a></i>)</small></p>","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.1","dataType":{"id":"DT-ShortString"},"format":"plain"},{"id":"PC-Description","changedAt":"2023-05-22T22:54:51.783Z","title":"dcterms:description","description":[{"text":"<p>An account of the resource. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description\">DCMI</a></i>)</small></p><p>Descriptive text (reference: Dublin Core) about resource represented as rich text in XHTML content. SHOULD include only content that is valid and suitable inside an XHTML 'div' element. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://open-services.net/\">OSLC</a></i>)</small></p>","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.1","dataType":{"id":"DT-Text"},"format":"xhtml"},{"id":"PC-Type","changedAt":"2025-03-06T15:04:02.280Z","title":"dcterms:type","description":[{"text":"<p>The nature or genre of the resource. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type\">DCMI</a></i>)</small></p><p>Recommended best practice is to use a controlled vocabulary such as the DCMI Type Vocabulary [DCMITYPE]. To describe the file format, physical medium, or dimensions of the resource, use the Format element.</p><p>For example, a [[FMC:Actor]] may represent a <i>System Function</i>, a <i>System Component</i> or a <i>User Role</i>. Similarly, in the context of process modelling, a FMC:Actor may represent a <i>Process Step</i> or again a <i>User Role</i>. So, all of these are meaningful values for a FMC:Actor's property named dcterms:type.</p>","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.1","dataType":{"id":"DT-String-LE32"},"format":"plain"},{"id":"PC-Diagram","changedAt":"2023-02-26T14:40:17.601Z","title":"SpecIF:Diagram","description":[{"text":"A diagram illustrating the resource or a link to a diagram.","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.1","dataType":{"id":"DT-Text"},"multiple":true,"format":"xhtml"},{"id":"PC-Notation","changedAt":"2023-02-26T21:06:48.930Z","title":"SpecIF:Notation","description":[{"text":"The notation used by a model diagram, e.g. 'BPMN 2.0', 'SysML Activity Diagram' or 'FMC Block Diagram'.","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.2","dataType":{"id":"DT-String-LE32"},"format":"plain"},{"id":"PC-UmlIsservice","changedAt":"2024-07-09T12:03:24.570Z","title":"uml:is_Service","revision":"1.2","dataType":{"id":"DT-Boolean"}},{"id":"PC-UmlFlowdirection","changedAt":"2024-07-09T05:23:08.410Z","title":"uml:Flow_Direction","revision":"1.2","dataType":{"id":"DT-String-LE32"},"format":"plain"}],"resourceClasses":[{"id":"RC-Paragraph","changedAt":"2024-03-02T20:55:23.295Z","title":"SpecIF:Paragraph","description":[{"text":"<p>A 'Paragraph' is an unspecified information in a document at any level.</p>","language":"en"},{"text":"<p>Ein 'Textabschnitt' in einem Dokument auf beliebiger Ebene.</p>","language":"de"}],"revision":"1.1","instantiation":["auto","user"],"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Name"},{"id":"PC-Description"},{"id":"PC-Diagram"},{"id":"PC-Type"}]},{"id":"RC-PigElement","changedAt":"2025-11-11T14:39:03.478Z","title":"pig:Element","description":[{"text":"An abstract superclass for pig:Organizer, pig:Entity and pig:Relationship"}],"revision":"2.0","instantiation":[],"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Name"},{"id":"PC-Description"},{"id":"PC-Type"}]},{"id":"RC-PigOrganizer","changedAt":"2025-09-23T07:15:25.794Z","title":"pig:Organizer","description":[{"text":"A hierarchical organizer such as an outline or diagram referencing model-elements."}],"revision":"2.0","instantiation":["auto","user"],"extends":{"id":"RC-PigElement"}},{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement","changedAt":"2025-03-08T20:23:37.245Z","title":"SpecIF:ModelElement","description":[{"text":"Is a generalized type for model elements.","language":"en"},{"text":"Ist ein generalisierter Typ für Modellelemente.","language":"de"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"&#x2606;","instantiation":["auto"],"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Name"},{"id":"PC-Description"},{"id":"PC-Type"}]},{"id":"RC-SpecifView","changedAt":"2025-08-15T19:41:37.282Z","title":"pig:View","description":[{"text":"<p>A 'Model View' is a graphical diagram with a specific communication purpose, e.g. a business process or system composition. A suitable notation is applied.</p>"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"▣","instantiation":["auto","user"],"extends":{"id":"RC-Paragraph"},"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Notation"}]},{"id":"RC-Actor","changedAt":"2025-03-08T20:21:05.195Z","title":"FMC:Actor","description":[{"text":"<p>An 'Actor' is a fundamental model element type representing an active entity, be it an activity, a process step, a function, a system component or a role.</p><p>The  particular use or original type is specified with a [[dcterms:type]] property of the 'FMC:Actor'. A value of that property should be an ontology-term, such as [[bpmn:processStep]].</p>","language":"en"},{"text":"<p>Ein 'Akteur' ist ein fundamentaler Modellelementtyp, der eine aktive Entität darstellt, sei es eine Aktivität, ein Prozessschritt, eine Funktion, eine Systemkomponente oder eine Rolle.</p><p>Die spezielle Verwendung oder der ursprüngliche Typ wird mit einer [[dcterms:type]] Eigenschaft von 'FMC:Actor' spezifiziert. Die Werte dieser Eigenschaft können Ontologiebegriffe sein, wie z.B. [[bpmn:timer]].</p>","language":"de"},{"text":"<p>Un 'Acteur' est un type d'élément de modèle fondamental représentant une entité active, qu'il s'agisse d'une activité, d'une étape de processus, d'une fonction, d'un composant de système ou d'un rôle.</p><p>L'utilisation particulière ou le type original est spécifié avec une propriété [[dcterms:type]] de 'FMC:Actor'. Les valeurs de cette propriété peuvent être des termes d'ontologie, tels que [[bpmn:timer]].</p>","language":"fr"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"&#x25A1;","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"}},{"id":"RC-Collection","changedAt":"2024-06-09T18:27:41.176Z","title":"SpecIF:Collection","description":[{"text":"<p>A 'Collection' is a logical (often conceptual) group of resources linked with a [[SpecIF:contains]] statement. It corresponds to a <a href=\"https://camunda.com/bpmn/reference/\">'Group'</a> in BPMN Diagrams.</p><p>BPMN: An arbitrary set of objects can be defined as a Group to show that they logically belong together. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://www.bpmn-tool.com/en/tutorial/\">BPMN Tutorial</a></i>)</small></p>","language":"en"},{"text":"<p>Eine 'Kollektion' ist eine logische Gruppierung bestimmter Modellelemente, die per [[SpecIF:contains]] Relation zusammen gefasst sind. Sie entspricht einer <a href=\"https://camunda.com/bpmn/reference/\">'Gruppe'</a> in BPMN Diagrammen. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://www.bpmn-tool.com/en/tutorial/\">BPMN Tutorial</a></i>)</small></p>","language":"de"},{"text":"<p>Une 'collection' est un groupe logique (souvent conceptuel) de ressources liées par une déclaration [[SpecIF:contains]]. Elle correspond à un <a href=\"https://camunda.com/bpmn/reference/\">'groupe'</a> dans les diagrammes BPMN. <small>(<i>source: <a href=\"http://www.bpmn-tool.com/en/tutorial/\">BPMN Tutoriel</a></i>)</small></p>","language":"fr"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"⬚","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"}},{"id":"RC-State","changedAt":"2025-03-08T20:04:01.555Z","title":"FMC:State","description":[{"text":"<p>A 'State' is a fundamental model element type representing a passive entity, be it a value, a condition, an information storage or even a physical shape.</p><p>The particular use or the original type is specified with a [[dcterms:type]] property of the 'FMC:State'. A value of that property should bean  ontology-term, such as [[bpmn:dataObject]].</p>","language":"en"},{"text":"<p>Ein 'Zustand' ist ein fundamentaler Modellelementtyp, der eine passive Entität darstellt, sei es ein Wert, ein Dokument, ein Informationsspeicher, eine Bedingung oder eine physische Beschaffenheit.</p><p>Die spezielle Verwendung oder der ursprüngliche Typ wird mit einer [[dcterms:type]] Eigenschaft von 'FMC:State' spezifiziert. Die Werte dieser Eigenschaft können Ontologiebegriffe sein, wie z.B. [[ArchiMate:DataObject]].</p>","language":"de"},{"text":"<p>Un 'État' est un type d'élément de modèle fondamental représentant une entité passive, qu'il s'agisse d'une valeur, d'une condition, d'un stockage d'informations ou même d'une forme physique.</p><p>L'utilisation particulière ou le type original est spécifié avec une propriété [[dcterms:type]] de 'FMC:State'. Les valeurs de cette propriété peuvent être des termes d'ontologie, tels que [[ArchiMate:DataObject]].</p>","language":"fr"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"&#x25CB;","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"}},{"id":"RC-Event","changedAt":"2025-03-08T19:57:15.384Z","title":"FMC:Event","description":[{"text":"<p>An 'Event' is a fundamental model element type representing a time reference, a change in condition/value or more generally a synchronization primitive.</p><p>The particular use or the original type is specified with a [[dcterms:type]] property of the 'FMC:Event'. A value of that property should be an ontology-term, such as [[bpmn:startEvent]].</p>","language":"en"},{"text":"<p>Ein 'Ereignis' ist ein fundamentaler Modellelementtyp, der eine Zeitreferenz, eine Änderung einer Bedingung/eines Wertes oder allgemeiner ein Synchronisationsmittel darstellt.</p><p>Die spezielle Verwendung oder der ursprüngliche Typ wird mit einer [[dcterms:type]] Eigenschaft von 'FMC:Event' spezifiziert. Die Werte dieser Eigenschaft sollen Ontologiebegriffe sein, wie z.B. [[bpmn:startEvent]].</p>","language":"de"},{"text":"<p>Un 'Événement' est un type d'élément de modèle fondamental représentant une référence temporelle, un changement de condition/valeur ou plus généralement une primitive de synchronisation.</p><p>L'utilisation particulière ou le type original est spécifié avec une propriété [[dcterms:type]] de 'FMC:Event'. Les valeurs de cette propriété peuvent être des termes d'ontologie, tels que [[bpmn:startEvent]].</p>","language":"fr"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"&#x2662;","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"}},{"id":"RC-Folder","changedAt":"2024-03-02T15:28:50.414Z","title":"SpecIF:Heading","description":[{"text":"A 'Heading' is a chapter title at any level with optional description.","language":"en"},{"text":"Eine 'Überschrift' in einem Dokument ist der Titel eines Kapitels. Sie kann eine Beschreibung haben, die als Einleitung oder Zusammenfassung des Kapitels genutzt werden kann.","language":"de"}],"revision":"1.1","instantiation":["auto","user"],"extends":{"id":"RC-Paragraph"},"isHeading":true},{"id":"RC-UmlDiagram","changedAt":"2025-11-09T11:47:24.726Z","title":"pig:View","description":[{"text":"<p>A 'Diagram' is a graphical model view with a specific communication purpose, e.g. a business process or system composition.</p>"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"▣","instantiation":["auto"],"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Name"},{"id":"PC-Description"},{"id":"PC-Diagram"},{"id":"PC-Type"},{"id":"PC-Notation"}]},{"id":"RC-UmlClass","changedAt":"2024-08-29T13:56:10.140Z","title":"SpecIF:ModelElement","description":[{"text":"Is a generalized type for model elements.","language":"en"},{"text":"Ist ein generalisierter Typ für Modellelemente.","language":"de"}],"revision":"1.2","icon":"&#x2606;","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"}},{"id":"RC-UmlPackage","changedAt":"2024-06-13T07:55:07.739Z","title":"uml:Package","revision":"1.2","instantiation":["auto","user"],"extends":{"id":"RC-Collection"},"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Name"},{"id":"PC-Description"}],"isHeading":true},{"id":"RC-UmlPort","changedAt":"2024-07-09T05:29:06.284Z","title":"uml:Port","revision":"1.2","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"RC-Actor"},"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-UmlIsservice"},{"id":"PC-UmlFlowdirection"}]},{"id":"RC-SysmlRequirement","changedAt":"2025-11-08T14:09:30.981Z","title":"IREB:Requirement","revision":"1.2","icon":"&#8623;","instantiation":["auto","user"],"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Name"},{"id":"PC-Description"},{"id":"PC-Type"}]}],"statementClasses":[{"id":"SC-SpecifRelates","changedAt":"2024-06-09T12:35:33.150Z","title":"SpecIF:relates","description":[{"text":"Is a generalized type for model relations.","language":"en"},{"text":"Ist ein generalisierter Typ für Modellrelationen.","language":"de"}],"revision":"1.2","instantiation":["auto"],"propertyClasses":[{"id":"PC-Type"}]},{"id":"SC-DctermsHaspart","changedAt":"2024-08-30T08:33:26.304Z","title":"dcterms:hasPart","description":[{"text":"A related resource that is included either physically or logically in the described resource.\n\n*Comment: This property is intended to be used with non-literal values. This property is an inverse property of [[dcterms:isPartOf]].*","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.2","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"SC-SpecifRelates"},"subjectClasses":[{"id":"RC-Actor"},{"id":"RC-State"},{"id":"RC-Collection"},{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},{"id":"RC-UmlClass"}],"objectClasses":[{"id":"RC-Actor"},{"id":"RC-State"},{"id":"RC-Collection"},{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},{"id":"RC-UmlPort"},{"id":"RC-UmlClass"}]},{"id":"SC-shows","changedAt":"2025-11-09T08:41:18.079Z","title":"SpecIF:shows","description":[{"text":"<p>A [[SpecIF:Diagram]] 'shows' a model element, e.g, a [[FMC:Actor]], [[FMC:State]], [[FMC:Event]] or [[SpecIF:Collection]].</p>\n<p>No eligible object classes are specified, so all resources and statements are eligible. It would be a rather long list to include the classes of all eligible resources and statements which can be shown on a diagram - and it would have to be updated every time a new one is included in the ontology. Certainly, some semantic precision is given up, but in an acceptable way.</p>","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.1","instantiation":["auto"],"subjectClasses":[{"id":"RC-SpecifView"},{"id":"RC-UmlDiagram"}]},{"id":"SC-contains","changedAt":"2025-11-09T08:55:27.051Z","title":"SpecIF:contains","description":[{"text":"General containment, such as:\n- Package-A *contains* Diagram-B\n- Collection-1 *contains* DataObject-1.1\n\nNot to confound with *[[dcterms:hasPart]]*.","language":"en"}],"revision":"1.1","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"SC-SpecifRelates"},"subjectClasses":[{"id":"RC-Actor"},{"id":"RC-State"},{"id":"RC-Collection"},{"id":"RC-UmlPackage"}],"objectClasses":[{"id":"RC-Actor"},{"id":"RC-State"},{"id":"RC-Event"},{"id":"RC-Collection"},{"id":"RC-UmlPackage"},{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},{"id":"RC-SpecifView"},{"id":"RC-UmlDiagram"},{"id":"RC-SysmlRequirement"}]},{"id":"SC-SpecifIsassociatedwith","changedAt":"2024-07-17T14:56:18.430Z","title":"SpecIF:isAssociatedWith","description":[{"text":"<p>A [[FMC:State]] is associated with another [[FMC:State]] (e.g. a class is associated with another class, as shown in a UML Class Diagram).</p>","language":"en"}],"revision":"rev-10387758265","instantiation":["auto"],"extends":{"id":"SC-SpecifRelates"}},{"id":"SC-SpecifIsspecializationof","changedAt":"2024-07-17T15:12:53.003Z","title":"SpecIF:isSpecializationOf","description":[{"text":"<p>A FMC:Actor is a specialization of another FMC:Actor; similarly for FMC:State and FMC:Event.</p>","language":"en"}],"revision":"rev-9054557983","instantiation":["auto"]}],"files":[{"id":"F-9716257805","title":"files_and_images/CASCaRA Metamodel Diagram.png","type":"image/png","changedAt":"2026-02-23T13:54:14.468Z"},{"id":"F-8369212006","title":"files_and_images/CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure Diagram.png","type":"image/png","changedAt":"2026-02-23T13:54:03.350Z"}],"resources":[{"id":"eee_1045467100313_135436_1","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-Folder"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"CASCaRA Metamodel and Semantic Infrastructure"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Author:PCUser.\nCreated:01.10.2012 15:10.\nTitle:.\nComment:.\n"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Model"}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-UmlPackage"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"CASCaRA Metamodel"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Package"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741251792687_379047_42601","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:28:46.369Z","revision":"rev-8834938144","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifView"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"CASCaRA Metamodel Diagram"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The following major design goals are pursued:\n- Separate syntax and semantics: The metamodel governs the graph pattern independently of the ontology. Any software depends on the metamodel and doesn’t need updating, when the ontology evolves over time.\n- Simplify transformation: A graph pattern is designed which may be represented in RDF, JSON-LD, GQL and OOP alike. Bidirectional transformations between any of those formats shall be possible without data-loss. Admittedly this ‘sweet-spot’ has reduced expressivity when compared with any of the listed data formats, but the choice of implementation technologies is maximized. Verification and validation will show that the resulting expressivity of the graph is sufficient for the purpose.\n\nThe metamodel is a 'platform independent model' in OMG terms and defines both the classes (above the dashed line) and their instances (below the dashed line) for the CASCaRA Product Information Graph. Both the classes and the instances are data:\n- [[Entity]] and [[anEntity]] are used for model elements, such as a requirement, a function or a system component. \n- [[Relationship]] and [[aRelationship]] are used for relations between elements, such as a 'system component satisfies a requirement'. A relationship class may define the classes of entities or relationships, whose instances are eligible as source or target in a directed relationship.\n- Every [[Entity]] and [[Relationship]] can define an individual set of [[Property]], each of which specifies a data type and range. For example, a requirement might have three properties, such as a „Title“ with data type „String of max. length 96“, a „Description“ with data type „String“ without restriction and a „Priority“ with data type „String with a single choice of ['high', 'medium', 'low']“.\n- A datatype may be any of those known from XML. As described above, some parameters may restrict the value range, such as minimum and/or maximum value of a  number, a string length or a set of enumerated values. \n- [[anEntity]] or [[aRelationship]] is an instance of [[Entity]] or [[Relationship]] respectively. Each instance usually has a set of [[aProperty]] corresponding with the [[Property]] of its class.\n\nNote:\n- \"Technical\" super-class and sub-class refer to the UML elements used in this metamodel by means of UML:Generalization.\n- \"Semantic\" super-class and sub-class refer to associations between the real world instances of the metamodel items as specified by the UML associations named 'specializes'.\n- As usual, the classes with white background and italic name are abstract."}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Diagram"},"values":[[{"text":"<object data=\"files_and_images/CASCaRA Metamodel Diagram.png\" type=\"image/png\">files_and_images/CASCaRA Metamodel Diagram.png</object>"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Diagram"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Notation"},"values":[[{"text":"UML Class Diagram"}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771671893915_815790_18471","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Item"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The technical super-class of all CASCaRA metamodel items specifying the type of item to allow for simple schema checking and transformation.\n\nDetails:\n- The class is abstract.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771672787619_626535_18519","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"itemType"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Here it is modeled as a string, but in fact it is an enumeration containing all concrete metamodel items (represented as UML classes), thus [Link, Property, Entity, Relationship, aPackage, aSourceLink, aTargetLink, aProperty, anEntity, aRelationship]."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776602722_98160_44400","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Identifiable"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"All technical sub-classes of this class are identifiable, means they have an identifier, a title (name) and optionally a description. \n\nDetails:\n- The class is abstract.\n- All attributes are inherited by its subclasses.\n- All class level items in the upper part of the diagram are commonly released and made available with an URL path including the revision. Hence, multiple revisions of the class set may exist in parallel.\n- All instance level items in the lower part of the diagram may have individual revisions with their respective revision, modification date and creator. The prior revision identifier is memorized to support change history and branching. In case of a merge, there are two prior revisions.\n\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776960082_840084_44503","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"id"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1751542746757_462879_42095","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"title"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1751542884336_630426_42099","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"description"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741777831234_907290_44608","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Element"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A technical super-class of [[Entity]] (class of entities) and [[Relationship]] (class of relationships). \n\nDetails:\n- The class is abstract.\n- All attributes and associations are inherited by its technical sub-classes Entity and Relationship.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776386192_365428_44395","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"icon"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"An icon defined with a class can be used to decorate the instances.\n\nExample: \n- Folders as sub-class of Organizer and thus Entity may specify a UTF-8 character 🗀 for use by folders grouping certain model-elements.\n- A data-URL of an icon is also permitted."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741252869188_614_42852","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Every class [[Entity]] and [[Relationship]] can have an individual set of configurable properties, each of which is uniquely defined by datatype and range. A Property is an owl:ObjectProperty when enumeratedValues are defined and is an owl:DatatypeProperty otherwise.\n\nExample: A requirement might have a list with three properties, such as \n- *Title* with data type „String of max. length 96“, \n- *Description* with data type „String“ wíthout length restriction and \n- *Priority* with data type „String with a single choice of ['high', 'medium', 'low']“.\n\nDetails:\n- Property class must have a title and may have a description named.\n- Property class may define a minimum and maximum count of values.\n- Property class must define a datatype and may restrict its range by minInclusive, maxInclusive or or a pattern defined by Regular Expression.\n-  Property class may define a set of enumerated values which must of course satisfy its own data type and range\n- A property class may define a default value which must of course satisfy its own data type and range.\n- Property class may be composed of multiple property classes to form a structured data type (xs:complexType). The structure must be a tree, thus without cyclic dependency.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1748952952204_277375_42119","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"datatype"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"One of the xs: data types. Shall be anyURI."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741259644097_123264_43470","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"minCount"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The minimal count an instance may have properties of this class. Is '0' by default."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741259741852_805697_43476","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"maxCount"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The maximal count an instance may have properties of this class. Is unbounded (infinite) by default."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1748949941816_8091_42095","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"maxLength"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Maximum length of a property value with datatype 'xs:string'. Is not allowed with any other datatype."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1748950213739_692776_42111","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"pattern"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A Regular Expression that must evaluate successfully with the property value. Can also be used to limit the number of decimals of a number, as there is no restriction like xs:fractionDigits in SHACL."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1748950030952_929749_42099","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"minInclusive"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The minimum value a property of this type may have. May be applied only for numeric datatypes.  It the intrinsic minimum value of the datatype by default."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1748950114069_51401_42103","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"maxInclusive"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The maximum value a property of this type may have. May be applied only for numeric datatypes. It the intrinsic maximum value of the datatype by default."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771688645413_401101_20413","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"enumeratedValue"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A property may be assigned zero to many values enumerated by its class. Enumerated values can be defined for all datatypes. By default all values in the range of the datatype can be assigned."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741260278956_301250_43534","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"defaultValue"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Optional default value(s) in case a modelElement's property does not have an individual value.  It must follow the definitions of the PropertyClass, of course.\n\nHere, the attribute is named 'sh:defaultValue' for clarity and may just be called 'values' in an implementation, as all restrictions and operations of a property's values apply."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771688746398_932479_20433","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"unit"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A unit as defined by the International System of Units (SI). A unit can only be defined for a numeric datatype. By default the property has no unit."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771688893681_342154_20442","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A Link is an identifiable link class. A Link is an owl:ObjectProperty.\n\nExample: \n- An Organizer (semantic sub-class of Entity) may list Model-Elements (another semantic sub-class of Entity) to provide a document outline.\n- As such the Link class *lists* is specified as enumeratedTargetLink by Organizer."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741332240391_169353_43869","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Entity is a class of model elements, such as a system component or a requirement. An Entity is an owl:Class.\n\nDetails:\n- Entity should have a title (name) and may have a description (definition).\n- Entity may specify (configure) zero to many classes of properties its instances may have. \n- The definitions of the entity together with those of the properties may be used to build user dialogs with input verification as well as to check its instances whether all property values have a correct type and value range as well as whether all required ones are present.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741251882847_25282_42662","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Relationship"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Relationship is a class of relationships between two entities to allow assertions such as 'a system component satisfies a requirement'. All relationships are bilateral and directed. This allows for statements according to propositional logic. They can be easily mapped to many technologies such as RDF or even ReqIF. Being reified, a Relationship is an owl:Class.\n\nDetails:\n- Relationship must have a title (name) and may have a description (definition).\n- Relationship lists zero to many property classes its instances may have.\n- Relationship may define (configure) entitiy classes or relationship classes, whose instances are eligible as source resp. target in a relationship. If none are defined, all entities and relationships are eligible.\n- Relationship is reified (as a rdfs:Resource in RDF), so that it can be a source or target of another Relationship - to make a statement on a statement.\n- The definitions of a relationship together with those of their properties may be used to build user dialogs with input verfication and to check its instances whether all properties have a correct type and value range as well as whether all required ones are present.\n\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741860988628_327516_42251","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"anElement"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A technical superclass of [[anEntity]] and [[aRelationship]]. \n\nDetails:\n- The class is abstract.\n- All attributes and associations are inherited by its sub-classes.\n- Sub-classes may have individual revisions with revision id, modification date and creator. The prior revision id is memorized to support change history and branching. In case of a merge, there are two prior revisions.\n\n\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741777082773_650555_44513","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"modified"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A ISO-8601 DateTime value recording the point in time of the last change."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741777152479_29656_44527","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"revision"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A unique string identifying the revision of the entity or relationship instance."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1757615958224_290574_18448","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"priorRevision"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Links to the previous revisions of an entity or relationship instance. It is a list with \n- zero elements, if it is the first revision,\n- one element for a subsequent revision or\n- two elements when two branches are merged."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1748952227529_103968_42115","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"creator"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The person committing the last change. Is often an e-mail address."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741254707021_484850_42937","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"aProperty"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Each property belongs to a single [[Entity]] or [[Relationship]]. A property has *no* identifier, thus a property update results in a new revision of the element to which it belongs. Is 'payload' having a clear meaning through the respective Property class.\n\nDetails:\n- A property may be required or not depending on the attributes sh:minCount and sh:maxCount of its class, but an existing property must have a value.\n- A property may be composed of multiple properties to form a structured data set according to its [[Property]] class.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741259824343_252859_43498","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-State"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"value"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The value of a property.\n\nDetails:\n- If the datatype of the property's class is string, the value is a language string consisting of value and IETF language tag.\n- Otherwise the value is a simple value."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771676505284_159097_18793","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"aLink"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Is a technical super-class for link instances.\n\nDetails:\n- The class is abstract.\n- A list of enumerated endpoints (references) per link instance is possible.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771693616773_590056_21246","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"aSourceLink"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A link instance serving as source for a reified relationship.\n\nFrom a semantic point of view, there is no need to make a distinction between aSourceLink and aTargetLink at the metamodel level. The distinction can be done and *is* made at ontology level in the CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure. However it is much easier to check the pattern/schema/shape, if the metamodel item type is explicit.\n\nExample: \n- A single 'satisfies' relationship can relate one or many function instances to a requirement instance. "}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771693534418_96399_21170","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"aTargetLink"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A link instance serving as target for a reified relationship.\n\nFrom a semantic point of view, there is no need to make a distinction between aSourceLink and aTargetLink at the metamodel level. The distinction can be done and *is* made at ontology level in the CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure. However it is much easier to check the pattern/schema/shape, if the metamodel item type is explicit.\n\nExample: \n- A single 'satisfies' relationship can relate a function instance to one or multiple requirement instances (targets)."}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741332525039_556704_43936","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"anEntity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Is used for instances of model-elements such as a system component or a requirement. Is 'payload' having a clear meaning through the respective Entity class.\n\nDetails:\n- An entity must have either a title or a description - or both. This allows to compose documents including text paragraphs without title. \n- The entity's class enumerates the classes of properties it may have.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741252702146_888127_42789","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"aRelationship"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Class"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"Is used for relations between entities, such as a 'system component satisfies a requirement'. All relationships are bilateral and directed. Is 'payload' having a clear meaning through the respective Relationship class.\n\nDetails:\n- This is a reified graph edge and must have exactly one source and target entity each. The source must be an entity or relationship with a class defined by an eligible source class of its [[Relationship]]. The same applies for the target.\n- Even though a relationship instance may have an individual title, it is advised to omit it and assume its class' title when needed to assure that relationships of the same class are named equally.\n- The relationship's class enumerates the classes of properties it may have.\n"}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839451123_494221_23070","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-UmlPackage"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Package"}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771752202367_248750_18752","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:59:38.444Z","revision":"rev-9902692797","replaces":["rev-10463753209"],"class":{"id":"RC-SpecifView"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure Diagram"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure complements the CASCaRA Metamodel by further sub-classing its items. The idea is to keep the metamodel as simple as possible without sacrificing semantic precision.\n\nLet's consider the paradigma of separating syntax and semantics with the objective to shield the software from an ontology under evolution over time. In all likelihood, the CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure will be used by software for reasons of simplicity. Therefore it is advised to treat the semantic infrastructure similarly to the metamodel: Change it seldomly and keep it downward compatible. That is, software built assuming an older version shall not break when a new version is adopted). So the semantic infrastructure can be seen as an intermediary layer between metamodel and ontology which is managed like the metamodel.\n\nIn any case an ontology for use with the CASCaRA Metamodel SHALL sub-class the items of the CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure."}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Diagram"},"values":[[{"text":"<object data=\"files_and_images/CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure Diagram.png\" type=\"image/png\">files_and_images/CASCaRA Semantic Infrastructure Diagram.png</object>"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"uml:Diagram"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Notation"},"values":[[{"text":"UML Class Diagram"}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771837566786_561798_22900","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Property"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The semantic foundation for all Property (class) definitions. Is an owl:DatatypeProperty when the value is a literal or an owl:ObjectProperty when the value is a reference to an enumerated value."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771799885159_867928_20697","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The semantic foundation for all Link (class) definitions. Is an owl:ObjectProperty."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771799982665_554941_20735","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"lists"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A [[Link]] class for use by [[Outline]] to enumerate eligible [[Entity]] and/or [[Relationship]] classes."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771834015004_267129_21659","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"shows"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A [[Link]] class for use by [[View]] to enumerate eligible [[Entity]] and/or [[Relationship]] classes that are visible on a view (e.g. model-diagram)."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771834044123_574439_21691","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"depicts"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A [[Link]] class for use by [[View]] to enumerate eligible [[Entity]] and/or [[Relationship]] classes that can own a view (e.g. model-diagram)."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771835422007_928561_22405","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"sourceLink"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A [[Link]] class for use by [[View]] to enumerate eligible [[Entity]] and/or [[Relationship]] classes that can serve as a source of a [[Relationship]].\n\nBy further specializing this class, a speaking title can be given to a sourceLink, such as 'employee' in a 'worksFor' relationship being a specialization of [[Relationship]]."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771835450776_649823_22441","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"targetLink"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Link"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A [[Link]] class for use by [[View]] to enumerate eligible [[Entity]] and/or [[Relationship]] classes that can serve as a target of a [[Relationship]].\n\nBy further specializing this class, a speaking title can be given to a targetLink, such as 'employer' in a 'worksFor' relationship being a specialization of [[Relationship]]."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771752760974_602036_19203","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The semantic foundation for all Entity (class) definitions. Is an owl:Class."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771752831951_108969_19241","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Organizer"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"An Organizer is about *presenting* genuine [[Model-Element]]s with a target group of users in mind, for example a document outline, a table or a diagram."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771753846220_443638_19398","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Table"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A specialized [[Organizer]] with elements (cells) arranged two-dimensionally in columns and rows. Any element SHALL contain a reference to any [[Entity]] or [[Relationship]]. "}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771752885802_727120_19292","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Tree"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A specialized [[Organizer]] with elements (nodes) arranged in a strictly hierarchical manner. Any element SHALL contain a reference to any [[Entity]] or [[Relationship]]. "}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771799591355_130334_20352","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Outline"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A tree (hierarchical arrangement) of references to graph nodes (vertices) to create a reading sequence. Graph nodes include [[Entity]] and [[Relationship]]. Outline is used at any level of the tree like a directory folder or universally for section, chapter and paragraph of a document."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771753874116_117667_19434","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"View"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A specialized [[Organizer]] with elements displayed in two or three dimensions such as a model-diagram, 3D visualization or pie-chart. Any element SHOULD reference any [[Entity]] or [[Relationship]]. "}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771837234420_922328_22817","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Root"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A root class serves to anchor organizer structures in a data package. While a graph has no start and no end, a root instance with a subordinated organizer structure offers a way to explore the graph for a given purpose.\n\nExample:\n- A document outline anchored at a root element would define a document to read by auditors and perhaps another one for potential customers. \n- When querying all instances of class Root, a list of available documents is returned."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771754644456_936441_19664","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Model-Element"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A Model-Element is an artifact *representing* a genuine part of a system specification in contrast to an [[Organizer]] which is about *presenting* model-elements."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771754749869_479288_19765","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Actor"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A fundamental model-element class for actors (e.g. users, functions, systems, components, ...)."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771754990713_657669_19795","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"State"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A fundamental model-element class for states (e.g. system or process states, information, form, color, ...)."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771755001063_275991_19825","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Event"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A fundamental model-element class for events (e.g. environmental or process events, ...)."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771833620366_65608_21335","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Enumeration"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Entity"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"A finite list of values for Properties."}]]}]},{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771755778117_565607_20273","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"RC-SpecifModelelement"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Relationship"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"cas_meta:Relationship"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Description"},"values":[[{"text":"The semantic foundation for all Relationship (class) definitions. Is an owl:Class."}]]}]},{"id":"FolderGlossary-10391243923","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:27:24.094Z","class":{"id":"RC-Folder"},"properties":[{"class":{"id":"PC-Name"},"values":[[{"text":"Model Elements (Glossary)"}]]},{"class":{"id":"PC-Type"},"values":[[{"text":"SpecIF:Glossary"}]]}]}],"statements":[{"id":"S-contains-11841656102","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741251792687_379047_42601"}},{"id":"S-contains-8086947074","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741254707021_484850_42937"}},{"id":"S-comprises-9584607573","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-DctermsHaspart"},"subject":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741254707021_484850_42937"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741259824343_252859_43498"}},{"id":"S-contains-10638031100","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771693616773_590056_21246"}},{"id":"S-contains-11563792405","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776602722_98160_44400"}},{"id":"S-comprises-10556184510","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-DctermsHaspart"},"subject":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776602722_98160_44400"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776960082_840084_44503"}},{"id":"S-comprises-9066975583","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-DctermsHaspart"},"subject":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776602722_98160_44400"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1751542746757_462879_42095"}},{"id":"S-comprises-11545422876","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-DctermsHaspart"},"subject":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776602722_98160_44400"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1751542884336_630426_42099"}},{"id":"S-contains-12059696629","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741777831234_907290_44608"}},{"id":"S-comprises-9304313239","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-DctermsHaspart"},"subject":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741777831234_907290_44608"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741776386192_365428_44395"}},{"id":"S-contains-11027319882","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771688893681_342154_20442"}},{"id":"S-contains-10853238318","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771693534418_96399_21170"}},{"id":"S-contains-11559964332","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741332240391_169353_43869"}},{"id":"S-contains-11255391540","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id":"_19_0_3_71e0233_1741332525039_556704_43936"}},{"id":"S-contains-11186407153","changedAt":"2026-02-23T14:19:16.402Z","class":{"id":"SC-contains"},"subject":{"id":"_2024x_3_71e0233_1771839371696_26166_23059"},"object":{"id"